infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Logging the error: console.log vs structured JSON
  desc At 2am a machine must read your logs — free-form strings it cannot parse
  compares
    - label console.log
      children
        - label Free-form strings
          desc No timestamps, no levels, no request boundaries
        - label Unqueryable at scale
          desc A machine cannot parse free text — no filter, no group-by
        - label No correlation
          desc Nothing ties one request's lines together or follows it downstream
        - label Stack logged three times
          desc Catch-log-rethrow at every layer prints the same stack thrice
    - label Structured JSON logger (pino)
      children
        - label Each line a JSON object
          desc Your log platform parses it into queryable fields
        - label Query and filter
          desc Filter level >= warn, group by path, pull one requestId
        - label Levels drop prod noise
          desc debug/log/warn/error — prod stops paying to store debug
        - label Redaction + throughput
          desc pino redacts secrets and sustains far higher write rate
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
